WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:10.030
We use our hands to interact with
objects -- grab them, manipulate them,

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:15.099
and release them. In virtual reality, however, 
such fine-grain interaction with virtual

00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:19.480
objects is generally not possible.
The main constraint to successfully

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:23.230
render haptics for virtual objects in a
realistic way is that the controller

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:27.820
must be able to produce and endure human
scale forces during interaction and

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:32.200
persist in rendering feedback, especially
when grasping and squeezing objects when

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.460
the forces on the controller are the highest.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:37.960
We present the CapstanCrunch --

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:42.180
the haptic controller that uses
controlled brake technology to render

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:47.620
haptic grasp at varying compliance
levels and that can sustain human scale

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:52.960
grasping forces up to 20 Newtons. 
It does so by using capstan-based brake

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:58.380
for variable pure resistive forces and a
clutch cable spring that is capable of

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:02.720
outfitting the stored energy of a built-in spring.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:08.460
This duality -- capstan break plus clutched spring
-- creates a unique device that can go beyond

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:15.520
limitation of the binary break or a spring and
can simulate human scale forces.

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:20.450
In a simulation of a push button, 
the user finger reaches the surface of the

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:25.580
material represented by a brake and
pushes it in against a resistance of a

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:30.140
spring up until some point where the
brake is being released and the user

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:37.640
feels the operation of the click of the
button until the button reaches full brake.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:40.580
Another example of interaction

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:44.370
implemented with CapstanCrunch is an
assembly of toy construction block.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:49.140
There are three stages to the assembly.
First, the two blocks are brought

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:54.510
together by bringing the fingers closer.
In stage two, a force is applied to

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:58.410
connect the two blocks together. Once 
the blocks are connected the brakes comes

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:02.930
into full stop and then the finger retreats.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:08.160
Final example of interaction implemented
with CapstanCrunch allows user to cut

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:12.360
materials with the pair of scissors.
The gradual growth of the force due to

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:17.750
increase of the material lever length is
approximated by a set of discrete steps.

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:23.480
We presented CapstanCrunch, a haptic
controller for rendering grasping feedback

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:28.640
up to human scale forces. CapstanCrunch 
is built around novel linear adjustable

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:34.100
friction-based capstan brake that renders 
human scale forces without the use of large

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:39.540
high-force electrically-powered consumptive 
and expensive actuators.

